  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1243 PM MDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nLooking through the rest of the week, Wednesday still appears to be \nour most active day. Deeper moisture will allow for higher \ninstability across the plains, though morning cloud cover may \nintroduce a cap that delays storms until later. Heavy rain will be a \nconcern across much of the area, with at least marginally severe \nstorms possible over the eastern plains again.\n\nThe upper ridge will amplify later in the week, slowly shifting to \nthe west. This will give us a slight warming/drying trend through \nSaturday, though scattered showers and storms will still be possible \nover and near the terrain each day. The plains may see a few storms \nas well, but much more isolated in nature. Flash flooding will \ncontinue to be a concern over the burn scars. For temperatures, \nhighs will mostly be in the high 80s-90s, with a few areas out east \nwill likely hit the triple-digit mark.\n\nLater this weekend into early next week, long-range guidance is \nshowing signs for an upper low to track in from the Pacific \nNorthwest, which could bring a quick return to cooler and wetter \nconditions across the region.",
